# Thumbnails / resource forks
._*

##### Linux
.directory
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*
.Trash-*

##### File sync clients
.dropbox
.dropbox.attr
.dropbox.cache

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.2 Editors and IDEs
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

##### Visual Studio Code / VSCodium
# VSCodium is a rebuild of the same source and uses the same .vscode/ folder
# and *.code-workspace files, so it needs no rules of its own. The Cursor and
# Windsurf forks below also write .vscode/ alongside their own directories.
#
# The whole folder is ignored: developers bring their own extensions and
# settings. Note that adding a "!.vscode/settings.json" exception below would
# NOT work, because git does not descend into an ignored directory. Use
# ".vscode/*" plus the exception if that ever changes.
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Local History for Visual Studio Code
.history/

##### Cursor
# VS Code fork, so its editor state is the .vscode/ folder above. It has no
# editor-only files of its own; its agent rules, ignore and index files are
# listed under Cursor in section 3.

##### Windsurf
# VS Code fork (Codeium). Editor state is .vscode/ above; its agent rules and
# ignore files are listed under Windsurf in section 3.

##### Kiro
# Built on Code OSS, so editor state is .vscode/ above. Its specs and steering
# directory is listed under Kiro in section 3.

##### Zed
# Editor settings only. Zed's assistant does not add project files of its own.
.zed/

##### JetBrains
# Covers IntelliJ, RubyMine, PhpStorm, AppCode, PyCharm, CLion, Android Studio,
# WebStorm and Rider.
.idea/
.phpstorm.*
atlassian-ide-plugin.xml

##### Vim / Neovim
# Swap files
[._]*.s[a-v][a-z]
# Keep vector graphics: the swap pattern above also matches .svg files whose
# name begins with "." or "_". Comment out if you do not need vector files.
!*.svg
[._]*.sw[a-p]
[._]s[a-rt-v][a-z]
[._]ss[a-gi-z]
[._]sw[a-p]

# Persistent undo
*.un~

# Sessions
Session.vim
Sessionx.vim

# Project-local config read by :set exrc - machine specific
.exrc
.vimrc
.nvimrc
.nvim.lua
.lvimrc

# netrw history
.netrwhist

##### Code navigation (ctags, cscope)
# Index files generated on demand by Vim, Emacs, Sublime and others. Anchored
# to the repository root: unanchored, "tags" would match any directory or file
# of that name anywhere in the tree.
/tags
/TAGS
/cscope.*

##### Emacs
# -*- mode: gitignore; -*-
*~
\#*\#
/.emacs.desktop
/.emacs.desktop.lock
*.elc
auto-save-list
tramp
.\#*

##### Sublime Text
*.tmlanguage.cache
*.tmPreferences.cache
*.stTheme.cache

# Workspace files are user-specific
*.sublime-workspace

# Project files should be checked into the repository, unless a significant
# proportion of contributors will probably not be using Sublime Text
# *.sublime-project

##### Notepad++
# Notepad++ writes its session and periodic backups under %AppData%, not in the
# working tree. Its "backup on save" copies land next to the file as *.bak,
# which section 1.3 already covers. This catches a custom backup directory.
nppBackup/

##### NetBeans
# The whole project folder is ignored, consistent with the other editors above.
# A shared nbproject/project.xml carries machine-specific include paths and PHP
# interpreter settings, so it is not useful to other developers.
nbproject/
/nbbuild/
/nbdist/
.nb-gradle/
# A bare "dist/" is deliberately NOT listed: unanchored, it matches at any
# depth and silently swallows committed build output.

##### Eclipse / Eclipse PDT
.metadata
.project
.buildpath
local.properties
.settings/
.loadpath
.recommenders
# A bare "bin/" and "tmp/" are deliberately NOT listed: unanchored, they match
# at any depth and can swallow legitimate plugin directories. If you need them,
# anchor them to the repository root:
# /bin/
# /tmp/

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.3 Backup and scratch files
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: "backups/" with an s. Do NOT change this to "backup/" - that is a
# Moodle plugin subdirectory holding course backup and restore code, and it
# must stay tracked.
backups/
*.bak
*.backup
*.old
*.ori
*.orig
*.original
*.tmp
*.temp

# Log files
*.log

